From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: cpr3-npu: build against mainline kernels

The CPR3 NPU regulator driver calls register_low_temp_notif() (a QSDK TSENS
low-temperature notifier that does not exist in mainline) and defines
cpr3_npu_temp_notify() without a prototype, both of which break the build
under -Werror. The cold-temperature open-loop voltage adjustment is optional,
so provide a no-op stub for the notifier and make the callback static. This
lets CONFIG_REGULATOR_CPR3_NPU be enabled so the NSS/NPU power island corner
rail (npu_corner, fed by PMIC s4) can be managed.

--- a/drivers/regulator/cpr3-npu-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/cpr3-npu-regulator.c
@@ -113,7 +113,17 @@
 
 struct cpr3_controller *g_ctrl;
 
-void cpr3_npu_temp_notify(int sensor, int temp, int low_notif)
+/*
+ * OpenWrt: the QSDK TSENS low-temperature notifier API is absent on mainline.
+ * Stub it as a no-op so the optional cold-temp open-loop voltage adjustment
+ * compiles; NSS core bring-up does not depend on cold-temp correction.
+ */
+static inline void register_low_temp_notif(int sensor, int cold_temp,
+					   void (*cb)(int, int, int))
+{
+}
+
+static void cpr3_npu_temp_notify(int sensor, int temp, int low_notif)
 {
 	u32 prev_sensor_state;
 
